The Munchkinland Murder        NannyMUD Times                        Page 13
Myster by the Old Quester

  When exploring a field east of Elm Road I noticed some wagon tracks that
  lead to an old farmhouse. Upon entering the farmhouse I found myself hurled
  into another place by a freak violent weather condition. I paid a visit to
  the town mayor in hopes of some advise on finding my way back home, which by
  the way is not as difficult as it may seem so don't panic, just be observant.
  While in his office I ended up hearing a very sad tale indeed.  It seems
  that many years ago there was a family that lived in a mansion some distance
  from town. Most folks didn't even realize they lived there as the mansion
  was quite secluded and the people must have valued their privacy.  Recently
  it was discovered that the entire family and staff were murdered.  The mayor
  is seeking help to clear it up and offering a nice reward for the effort.
  
  I made a brief visit to the old mansion before making my return trip to
  Larstown. I discovered it to be filled with unhappy ghosts who were indeed
  looking for answers as to what happened to them.  Each seemed to have met a
  unique demise. Some of them  are a bit reluctant to ask for help and were
  difficult to find,  yet they all seem appreciative to be shown items  that
  may jog their memories as to what happened.  In my first short visit I was
  not able to find all of the ghosts, but the mayor was confident that my
  memory was good enough concerning what I had discovered that I would not need to
  repeat what I had already done.  After several visits,  I gathered
  sufficient information and told the mayor who I thought had committed the
  murders, and then was given what was needed to collect my reward.

